virglrenderer: Venus makes an image that aliases one plane of a disjoint YCbCr image on MoltenVK

What: an image of a one-plane format with DISJOINT and ALIAS (the image that aliases one
plane of a disjoint multi-planar image) whose format query the driver answers with
FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED is asked once more without DISJOINT. That answer counts: in
vkCreateImage's check and the three vkGetDeviceImage* queries (vkr_image_info_ok), and in
what the guest is told by vkGetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties and
vkGetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties2 (on a copy of the guest's info). The create info
goes to the driver as the guest sent it. Only after a "no" and only for a format vkr's
table knows with one plane: a driver that answers the flags itself (KosmicKrisp) keeps
its answer. One-plane DISJOINT without ALIAS and multi-planar DISJOINT are not changed.
The refusal log line names the flags asked too.
Why: dEQP-VK.ycbcr.plane_view.memory_alias.*_fragment makes such an image (VUID-
VkImageCreateInfo-format-01577 allows it) and binds it with PLANE_0 to a plane's memory.
MoltenVK 1.4.2's format query refuses DISJOINT on every format that is not multi-planar
and does not look at ALIAS (MVKDevice.mm:1578), so vkr refused the create: 349 of the 400
cases failed with VK_ERROR_FORMAT_NOT_SUPPORTED on the M4 (3.2.18, 3.2.19, #693). MoltenVK's
vkCreateImage makes the image with one memory binding, as without DISJOINT (MVKImage.mm:
1261). Driver probe on the M4, 400 cases x (3 plain, 3 libgmalloc, 1 Metal validation):
0 crashes, 0 validation errors; MoltenVK says yes to 388 without DISJOINT, makes all 388
with it, with the same memory requirements as without (also asked with PLANE_0), and the
bytes written through the alias are the plane's in all 349 cases dEQP runs. KosmicKrisp
answers DISJOINT|ALIAS as without DISJOINT in 400 of 400 (3 + 3 runs). dEQP asks the query
only for the multi-planar format (VUID-VkImageCreateInfo-imageCreateMaxMipLevels-02251
wants one for the alias too); the guest is told what vkCreateImage does either way.
Upstream: OmacVM policy; nothing posted to MoltenVK.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-image-limits.c (bind-alias-* now on MoltenVK too, the
agree-* and devreq-alias cases).

